# Aurora Database Activity Streams (DAS) Architecture

## Overview

This project demonstrates how Amazon Aurora Database Activity Streams (DAS) securely captures every database activity, encrypts it, streams it through Amazon Kinesis, and processes it for security monitoring.

The implementation is divided into **two phases**:

- **Phase 1** – Understand how Aurora encrypts DAS records by manually decrypting them.
- **Phase 2** – Build the production monitoring pipeline described in the AWS reference architecture.

---

# Overall Architecture

```text
                             SQL Statements
                                   │
                                   ▼
                      Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL
                                   │
                  Database Activity Streams (DAS)
                                   │
                    (Encrypted Activity Records)
                                   │
                                   ▼
                         Amazon Kinesis Stream
                                   │
                 ┌─────────────────┴──────────────────┐
                 │                                    │
                 ▼                                    ▼
     Firehose (Raw Archive)              Firehose (Parsed Pipeline)
        No Lambda                            Lambda Transformation
                 │                                    │
                 ▼                                    ▼
      raw-encrypted/                         parsed/
      (Encrypted Records)                (Readable JSON Events)
                 │                                    │
                 ▼                                    ▼
        decrypt_record.py                     SNS Alerts
                 │                            Security Monitoring
                 ▼
      Original Database Activity
```

